Changes to the upstream code:
- src/extension.ts: removed the sponsorship prompt.
- src/pdf-viewer-provider.ts, src/pdf-document.ts: editable custom editor
  (annotation save, save as, revert, backup) and a typed message bridge.
- assets/main.mjs: ported to TypeScript as src/webview/main.ts and extended.
- package.json: new extension identity, view type and settings namespace.
All other new functionality lives in new files under src/ and assets/panel.css.

This product bundles PDF.js (https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js),
Copyright Mozilla Foundation, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(see assets/pdf.js/LICENSE), with the modifications in patches/pdf.js.patch.

ParaRead Android modifications (2026):
- Reuse src/webview TypeScript modules, src/messages.ts, languages.ts, webview strings.
- main.ts, sentence-store.ts, panel.ts, translation-client.ts: Android host,
  Room page caches, bounded page state, streamed drafts, reading restoration
  and durable whole-document job recovery.
- messages.ts, pdfjs.d.ts and tsconfig.json: Android message/typing/build changes.
- pointer-select.ts and panel.ts: touch gestures and pointer type handling.
- save-bridge.ts: native incremental save and annotation change observation.
- PDF.js ChunkedStream, range completion, SaveDocument/incrementalUpdate and
  viewer page buffer are patched during asset generation; patches are in
  scripts/patch_pdfjs.mjs and scripts/build_reader.mjs.
